comphelper: under LOK a snapshot names the checks around its longest gap

Patch 0121's timings showed PPTX snapshots on Windows running 100 to
190 ms between two checks, while DOCX ones stayed under 25 ms; they did
not say where. checkSnapshot takes the caller's source location by
default, so no caller changes, and the log line gives the file and line
of the checks that bound the longest gap and of the last one.
--- a/include/comphelper/snapshot.hxx
+++ b/include/comphelper/snapshot.hxx
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #pragma once
 
 #include <comphelper/comphelperdllapi.h>
+#include <source_location>
 
